Fix out-of-bounds read in tre_parse_bracket_items on a bracket
expression whose last pattern byte is '-'.

A bytes-mode pattern ending in a hyphen inside an unterminated bracket
expression, such as the 3-byte pattern "[a-", makes the parser read one
element past the end of the pattern buffer:

    ==1==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow
    READ of size 4
        #0 tre_parse_bracket_items src/extra/tre/tre-parse.c:365
        #1 tre_parse_bracket       src/extra/tre/tre-parse.c:453
        #2 tre_parse               src/extra/tre/tre-parse.c:1388
        #3 tre_compile             src/extra/tre/tre-compile.c:1920
        #4 tre_regncompb           src/extra/tre/regcomp.c:118
        #5 do_grepraw              src/main/grep.c:1739

The range check for a hyphen peeks at the following element,
"*(re + 1) != CHAR_RBRACKET", without first testing that one exists.
Every other lookahead in the parser is guarded by a comparison against
ctx->re_end; this one relies on the pattern buffer carrying a
terminating nul instead.  tre_regncomp() supplies that nul (it
allocates n + 1 elements and writes L'\0' at the end), but the
bytes-mode entry point tre_regncompb() -- used by grepRaw() and by
every useBytes = TRUE regex call -- allocates exactly n elements and
no terminator, so the peek at the final hyphen reads past the
allocation.

Guard the lookahead like the others.  Treating "no following element"
the same as "not a closing bracket" preserves the result the
nul-terminated path already produces (REG_ERANGE for "[a-", REG_OK for
"[a-]" and "[-a]").

Reachable from R via grepRaw(), and via grep(), sub(), regexpr() and
friends with useBytes = TRUE, whenever the pattern comes from an
untrusted source:

    grepRaw("[a-", charToRaw("xa-"), all = TRUE)

Found by fuzzing R with libFuzzer + AddressSanitizer.

Upstream status: NOT YET REPORTED to the R Bugzilla as of 2026-10-08.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

--- a/src/extra/tre/tre-parse.c
+++ b/src/extra/tre/tre-parse.c
@@ -362,8 +362,8 @@
 	  else
 	    {
 	      DPRINT(("tre_parse_bracket:   char: '%.*" STRF "'\n", REST(re)));
-	      if (*re == CHAR_MINUS && *(re + 1) != CHAR_RBRACKET
-		  && ctx->re != re)
+	      if (*re == CHAR_MINUS && ctx->re != re
+		  && (re + 1 >= ctx->re_end || *(re + 1) != CHAR_RBRACKET))
 		/* Two ranges are not allowed to share and endpoint. */
 		status = REG_ERANGE;
 	      min = max = *re++;
